# What must never reach an image.
#
# Docker's COPY does NOT honour .gitignore. This file is the only thing that
# stops a local .env or a working database being baked into a published image,
# and this repository has already been bitten by exactly that: ToolGate keeps
# its data inside its own package directory, so `COPY toolgate ./toolgate`
# shipped a developer's real credentials to the registry.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with **/ deliberately. A bare `.env` matches only
# the root of the build context, and the file that leaked was one level down.

# --- secrets and state ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/vault.key
**/*.pem
**/data
**/backups

# --- version control and CI ---
.git
.github
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes

# --- development only ---
**/tests
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build

# --- editor noise ---
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
